 year of sobriety McDonald decided it was  finally time to take on the Ironman were  you worried in any way it would  disappoint you know I started convincing  myself that I might not make it the week  of the race you see they start laying  the buoys for the swim course yeah and  just each day it's just going further  and further out he remembered the  hundreds of contributors who were  backing him and then I started thinking  well they didn't pay me to finish I just  said I was gonna do it then race day  finally came in Kona waking up that  morning and getting in the water wow  there's a powerful little bitter was  were you thinking about 20 years ago 25  yeah everything all of it you may not  know this but I'm a crier and I mean  literally I tears in my goggles  getting into the water so I was like you  know I came out of the water and I knew  uh what did you know I knew I had it in  12 hours and 42 minutes Michael McDonald  completed the 140 mile course  his wife Becky and their daughters were  there to greet him so how was Kona after  all these years of anticipating it it  was everything I dreamed it would be  well kids weddings you know the birth of  children those moments aside it was the  the best day of my life
 

